<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32984" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ŏrĭentālis</span></b> ,
			e, adj.
		oriens, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the
			East</i>, <i>Eastern</i>, <i>Oriental</i> (postclass.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">periculorum et operum orientalium socii,</span>”
				<i>in the East</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Just.
					14, 2, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">barba ria,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					12, 3, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">reges,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					38, 10, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">venti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 2, 22, 11</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Subst.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ŏrĭentā-les</span></b> ,
				ĭum, m., <i>the Orientals</i>, <i><span class="en">Just. 36, 3, 9</span></i>.—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ŏrĭentāles</span></b> ,
				ĭum, f. (sc. ferae), <i>wild beasts designed for hunting exhibitions</i>
			(as lions, tigers, panthers, etc.), <i><span class="en">Inscr.
				Murat. 654, 1</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
